mple graph.\\r\\n14: \\r\\n15: ## Main definitions\\r\\n16: \\r\\n17: - `SimpleGraph.eccent`: the eccentricity of a vertex in a simple graph, which is the maximum\\r\\n18:   distances between it and the other vertices.\\r\\n19: \\r\\n20: - `SimpleGraph.ediam`: the graph extended diameter, which is the maximum eccentricity.\\r\\n21:   It is `ℕ∞`-valued.\\r\\n22: \\r\\n23: - `SimpleGraph.diam`: the graph diameter, an `ℕ`-valued version of `SimpleGraph.ediam`.\\r\\n24: \\r\\n25: - `SimpleGraph.radius`: the graph radius, which is the minimum eccentricity. It is `ℕ∞`-valued.\\r\\n26: \\r\\n27: - `SimpleGraph.center`: the set of vertices with eccentricity equal to the graph's radius.\\r\\n28: \\r\\n29: -/\\r\\n30: \\r\\n31: @[expose] public section\\r\\n32: \\r\\n33: assert_not_exists Field\\r\\n34: \\r\\n35: namespace SimpleGraph\\r\\n36: variable {α : Type*} {G G' : SimpleGraph α}\\r\\n37: \\r\\n38: section eccent\\r\\n39: \\r\\n40: /-- The eccentricity of a vertex is the greatest distance between it and any other vertex. -/\\r\\n41: noncomputable def eccent (G : SimpleGraph α) (u : α) : ℕ∞ :=\\r\\n42:   ⨆ v, G.edist u v\\r\\n43: \\r\\n44: lemma eccent_def : G.eccent = fun u ↦ ⨆ v, G.edist u v := rfl\\r\\n45: \\r\\n46: lemma edist_le_eccent {u v : α} : G.edist u v ≤ G.eccent u :=\\r\\n47:   le_iSup (G.edist u) v\\r\\n48: \\r\\n49: lemma exists_edist_eq_eccent_of_finite [Finite α] (u : α) :\\r\\n50:     ∃ v, G.edist u v = G.eccent u :=\\r\\n51:   have : Nonempty α := Nonempty.intro u\\r\\n52:   exists_eq_ciSup_of_finite\\r\\n53: \\r\\n54: lemma eccent_eq_top_of_not_connected (h : ¬ G.Connected) (u : α) :\\r\\n55:     G.eccent u = ⊤ := by\\r\\n56:   rw [connected_iff_exists_forall_reachable] at h\\r\\n57:   push Not at h\\r\\n58:   obtain ⟨v, h⟩ := h u\\r\\n59:   rw [eq_top_iff, ← edist_eq_top_of_not_reachable h]\\r\\n60:   exact le_iSup (G.edist u) v\\r\\n61: \\r\\n62: lemma eccent_eq_zero_of_subsingleton [Subsingleton α] (u : α) : G.eccent u = 0 := by\\r\\n63:   simpa [