is directly comparable to that baseline rather than\\n12: being a differently-scored number.\\n13: \\n14: Why that matters here specifically: every formalization bug this repository has\\n15: found produced an *apparent success*. A model \\\"proved\\\" three items that were\\n16: `Fin 0` artefacts; another exploited `minCard`'s 0 fallback on an undefined\\n17: invariant. A stronger agent team is more likely to find such holes, not less, so\\n18: nothing is counted as resolved unless the kernel accepts it under an axiom\\n19: audit, and `--strict` additionally re-checks that the accepted direction agrees\\n20: with the ground-truth label the benchmark carries.\\n21: \\n22: Usage:\\n23:     python tools/antigravity_handoff.py export --partition gold --out handoff/\\n24:     # ... run /teamwork-preview over handoff/, save results into handoff/solved/\\n25:     python tools/antigravity_handoff.py verify --partition gold --dir handoff/solved\\n26: \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n27: from __future__ impor\\n<truncated 2857 bytes>\\n}\\\")\\n91:     print(f\\\"  brief:       {os.path.join(args.out, 'README.md')}\\\")\\n92:     print(f\\\"  put results in: {os.path.join(args.out, 'solved')}\\\")\\n93:     return 0\\n94: \\n95: \\n96: def _candidate_of(text: str):\\n97:     \\\"\\\"\\\"The `abbrev Candidate : Prop := …` body, normalised for comparison.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n98:     m = re.search(r\\\"abbrev\\\\s+Candidate\\\\s*:\\\\s*Prop\\\\s*:=(.*?)(?=\\\\n\\\\ntheorem )\\\", text, re.S)\\n99:     return re.sub(r\\\"\\\\s+\\\", \\\" \\\", m.group(1)).strip() if m else None\\n100: \\n101: \\n102: # ── admissibility ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\n103: #\\n104: # An answer is compiled as the *returned file*, helper lemmas included — pasting\\n105: # only the proof body back into the original, as the model campaign did, drops\\n106: # every lemma a real proof needs and turns a correct proof into \\\"unresolved\\\".\\n107: #\\n108: # Compiling the returned file is only sound if nothing in it can change what is\\n109: # being proved. The checks below close the routes that exist in Lean for that:\\n110: # editing `Candidate` or anything it elaborates against; extending its term past\\n111: # where it ended (a term does not stop at a newline); re-declaring `Candidate` or\\n112: # the target inside a namespace; adding `variable` hypotheses the target silently\\n113: # absorbs; redefining the tokens `Candidate` parses as; and bypassing the kernel.\\n114: # The target's type is then re-checked by Lean itself, and the axiom audit rejects\\n115: # `sorryAx` and anything non-standard.\\n116: \\n117: _CMD_START = (\\\"theorem\\\", \\\"lemma\\\", \\\"def\\\", \\\"abbrev\\\", \\\"example\\\", \\\"instance\\\", \\\"open\\\",\\n118:               \\\"set_option\\\", \\\"attribute\\\", \\\"noncomputable\\\", \\\"private\\\", \\\"protected\\\",\\n119:               \\\"@[\\\", \\\"#check\\\", \\\"#print\\\", \\\"structure\\\", \\\"inductive\\\", \\\"class\\\")\\n120: \\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\\n\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}\n12: {\"step_index\":131,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T18:38:18Z\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/benchmark/challenges_promising13/index.json\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"100\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing index.json\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View challenge index\\\"\"}}]}\n13: {\"step_index\":132,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"GENERIC\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T18:38:20Z\",\"content\":\"Created At: 2026-09-11T20:38:20+02:00\\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T20:38:20+02:00\\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/benchmark/challenges_promising13/ind